id: DRAFT-E655-scheme-bootstrap-generated-artifact-patch
category: build, recipe, portability
build_system: makefile|custom
phase: build
match_keywords: bootstrap compiler, scheme to c, generated c file, wget in Makefile, git clone in Makefile, OWLURL, can't find file to patch, patch generated file, apply_conandata_patches fails, build-time network, self-hosting build, radamsa, owl lisp, two-stage build, determinism of generated source
error_signature: "conan/CI build fails on 'Can't find file to patch' for a file that the upstream Makefile generates mid-build, or the build stalls/fails at a wget/curl/git clone step embedded in the upstream Makefile (OWLURL-style bootstrap downloads)"
error_excerpt: "patch: **** Can't find file to patch: radamsa.c (the file only exists after 'bin/ol -o radamsa.c rad/main.scm'); upstream Makefile also runs 'wget https://haltp.org/files/ol-0.2.2.c.gz' and 'git clone https://gitlab.com/owl-lisp/hex.git' during build"
root_cause: "Self-hosting projects compile a bootstrap tool first (here: Owl Lisp from a pinned precompiled C source), use it to generate the real source file (rad/*.scm -> radamsa.c), then compile the artifact. Package metadata systems assume all patched inputs exist before the build, so registering a patch against the generated file and applying it up front always fails; and upstream Makefiles that fetch the bootstrap/library over the network during build break hermetic CI builds."
rec_approach: "Vendor every build input in conandata.yml as separate keys (main tarball via sources:, bootstrap via e.g. owl_bootstrap:, library archive via hex_library:) and download them as raw files with sha256 verification; recreate the upstream layout in build() before compiling the bootstrap tool; run the generation step, then apply the platform patch to the just-generated file with 'patch -p1' from build(), and only then run the final compile. Keep the conandata patches: entry for metadata visibility but document why apply_conandata_patches() must NOT be called at build start. Prove determinism by building twice and comparing sha256 of the generated file before relying on the patch applying cleanly."
solution: "See archives/r/radamsa/0.7 (conanfile.py build() steps 1-5, conandata.yml owl_bootstrap/hex_library keys, patches/0001-radamsa-do_poll-ohos-chardev-writable.patch). Clean conan create round passes; the patch application is visible in conan-create.log ('RUN: patch -p1 ...', 'patching radamsa.c'); generated radamsa.c is byte-identical across independent builds (sha256 2d70a4ce...)."
fallback: "If the generator is not deterministic, pre-generate the artifact once, ship it as an extra source with its sha256, and patch it before the final compile (loses 'build from Scheme sources' fidelity; keep the generator inputs registered for provenance)."
prescan_pattern: "git clone.*Makefile|wget.*Makefile|Can't find file to patch"
verify_builds: "radamsa 0.7 on ohos-aarch64 (2026-09-22): clean conan create round G1/G2/G3 PASS, upstream tests/run 28/28, test_package 8/8; GitLab '-/archive/' endpoint 403s non-browser UAs while the API archive endpoint (api/v4/projects/<org>%2F<repo>/repository/archive.tar.gz?sha=<fullsha>) returns 200"
severity: 2
last_updated: 2026-09-22
